# dead_code.allow — repo-owned allow list for the fleet coding-discipline
# dead_code.py re-runs (MC 11430 audit CC-18; landed MC 11433). Format:
#   KIND path-or-name  reason   (matcher: whitespace-split, FIRST TWO tokens)
# ORPHAN-MODULE/DRIVERLESS rows match the reported rel-path; UNCALLED-FN rows
# match the method NAME (path:line drifts, names don't). Every row names why.
# DNA message subsystem (src/dna): the MC 11433 CC-16 keep/retire PARK is
# RETIRED by MC 11493 — owner ruling 2026-10-27 verbatim "I want tall to
# creature to be implemented since it is built" — the 5 parked methods
# (LanguageSignature.Generate + DnaLanguage Extract/Counter/ExtractCodon/Parse)
# gained their first product callers in world/WorldDirector.Talk.cs (the
# speak-key exchange, battery mode DNA_TALK); Speak ALREADY had a product caller
# since MC 1344 (TryInteract -> _dna.Speak, WorldDirector.cs) — which is why the
# audit never parked it; they must NOT reappear here.

